<p>The Dutch-flagged MV Hondius arrived Sunday near the Spanish port of Granadilla in the Canary Islands, escorted by a Civil Guard vessel, ahead of an evacuation and repatriation operation for most of the nearly 150 people on board after weeks at sea. The World Health Organization, Spanish authorities and ship operator Oceanwide Expeditions are coordinating the operation. Passengers and some crew were expected to be screened before direct transport to flights home. The outbreak has killed three passengers — a Dutch husband and wife and a German woman — and WHO has reported six confirmed cases and two probable or suspected cases linked to the ship. WHO officials said the Andes subtype was confirmed among those who tested positive; it is the only hantavirus type known to spread from person to person. The agency said everyone still on board was asymptomatic as of Saturday. WHO epidemic and pandemic preparedness director Maria Van Kerkhove said everyone on board should be treated as a high-risk contact and actively monitored for 42 days. She said the risk to the general public and to people in the Canary Islands remained low. WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus traveled to Tenerife to help oversee the evacuation and said the risk to local residents was low.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/I4fb_x9Fk1eeSTJQN49GqU5-73e-_asW4_hZCmzLQmD7cdFANR4yhOs4dH5zIUSxF-qd80yVvkpdJQ2UjBdaooieIDsmoYJGb1lsTlKjDi9_cgbyCN8xtVoNcfYh3VeyOPVrrPi1nwA9ODX9OxtSP3Q5mpx0J1seb8aQgwBCExI9GptNjSiwNybeh4kM4jeskMQTBznQQIgAfJ4SNz_iSUbI' alt='The MV Hondius arriving in Tenerife, Canary Islands, on Sunday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Evacuation route: Passengers are expected to move from the ship to shore by small boats, then travel through a cordoned-off route in sealed, guarded vehicles before boarding repatriation flights.</li><li>Port reception: Authorities set up a medical tent overnight at Granadilla as the shoreside reception area for the operation.</li><li>UK isolation: British health authorities prepared to receive about 24 people from the ship and isolate them in a hospital previously used for COVID-19 patients.</li></ul><blockquote>We classify everybody on board as what we call a high-risk contact - Maria Van Kerkhove</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Oceanwide Expeditions: After passengers and some crew disembark in Tenerife, the remaining crew are expected to take the vessel onward to the Netherlands. (<a href='https://www.iltempo.it/esteri/2026/05/10/news/hantavirus-nave-da-crociera-focolaio-tenerife-trasferimento-protetto-passeggeri-47654830/'>Il Tempo</a>)</li><li>Spanish/local officials: The Hondius was to remain at what officials described as the safest distance from the dock, instead of a routine pier-side disembarkation. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/eu-countries-prepare-repatriation-hantavirus-cruise-passengers/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Canary Islands residents: The evacuation prompted concern and demonstrations on the island. (<a href='https://www.rts.ch/info/monde/2026/article/hantavirus-le-paquebot-hondius-arrive-a-tenerife-sous-haute-surveillance-29237283.html'>RTS</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/health/hantavirus-hit-cruise-ship-spain-canary-islands/article70961627.ece'>Hantavirus-hit cruise ship arrives in Spain&#x27;s Canary Islands</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3353021/hantavirus-hit-cruise-ship-nears-canary-islands-who-led-evacuation'>Hantavirus-hit cruise ship reaches Spanish port for WHO-led evacuation</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/b5fdd84f-69bd-47ae-bd7b-df30ba3d758c'>Hantavirus cruise ship arrives in Tenerife for evacuation</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/countries-prepare-to-evacuate-hantavirus-ship-passengers1'>Countries prepare to evacuate hantavirus ship passengers</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://a